{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/library/11109","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"call number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300311706"}],"content":"ND653.G7 A3","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"repository number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404621"}],"content":"11109","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"The letters of a post-impressionist: being the familiar correspondence of Vincent van Gogh.","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[{"_label":"Gogh, Vincent van,","id":"actor/gogh-vincent-van","type":"Actor"},{"_label":"Houghton Mifflin Company","id":"actor/houghton-mifflin-company","type":"Actor"}],"timespan":{"_label":"1913","begin_of_the_begin":"1913-01-01T00:00:00Z","end_of_the_end":"1913-01-01T00:00:00Z","type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"Ephemera found between pp. xxx-xxxi : Etchings by John Marin exhibition checklist, E. Weyhe, March 13-31, 1921 ; enclosed : Eastman Kodak paper enclosed ; clipping of unknown article regarding Alfred Stieglitz at the Anderson Gallery.\nEphemera found inside : photograph by unknown photographer of [Alfred Stieglitz] and [Georgia O'Keeffe], undated.\nGeorgia O'Keeffe Personal Library.\nTranslated from the German by Anthony M. Ludovici.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"inscription statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435414"}],"content":"abq copy : fair condition.|SColl abq : Embossed stamp on front loose endpaper : Georgia O'Keeffe / Abiquiu, New Mexico.|SColl abq : Inscription from Alfred Stieglitz, January 21, 1918 : I read this volume when it came / out in 1913. - I had read it in / German some years before. - I just / ran across it amongst my books. - / You may have time to read - / and may not have read these letters. - / They'll interest you. - I want / you to have the book. - / It has been an endless Sunday to - / day - I have perhaps been over - / doing it lately - living too hard in / my own way - different from all / those about me - In touch but so / separated. - I'm glad you are / following the doctor's advice - / or orders. - The telegram came last / night after my letter had gone off. / To Georgia O'Keeffe - / a Little Girl - / from a very, very old man. - / '291' / Jan. 21, / 1918.","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[],"type":"HumanMadeObject"}